§ `Section 2027(b) and (c): limit on the value of allotments, and the manner of reducing them`

-- src:2710 | In any fiscal year, the Secretary shall limit the value of those allotments issued to an amount not in excess of the appropriation for such fiscal year. Notwithstanding any other provision of this chapter, if in any fiscal year the Secretary finds that the requirements of participating States will exceed the appropriation, the Secretary shall direct State agencies to reduce the value of such allotments to be issued to households certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program to the extent necessary to comply with the provisions of this subsection.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2027(b) (src:2710-2710)
GIVEN `the value of the allotments issued in the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the appropriation for the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2027(b) the value of the allotments issued is within the limit` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Secretary shall limit the value of those allotments issued to an amount not in excess of the appropriation for such fiscal year"
    IF `the value of the allotments issued in the fiscal year` GREATER THAN `the appropriation for the fiscal year` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:2710 | In any fiscal year, the Secretary shall limit the value of those allotments issued to an amount not in excess of the appropriation for such fiscal year. Notwithstanding any other provision of this chapter, if in any fiscal year the Secretary finds that the requirements of participating States will exceed the appropriation, the Secretary shall direct State agencies to reduce the value of such allotments to be issued to households certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program to the extent necessary to comply with the provisions of this subsection.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2027(b) (src:2710-2710)
GIVEN `the Secretary finds that the requirements of participating States will exceed the appropriation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2027(b) the Secretary is required to direct State agencies to reduce the value of the allotments to be issued` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if in any fiscal year the Secretary finds that the requirements of participating States will exceed the appropriation" (reading (a): a failed "if")
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the Secretary has made the finding is for the Secretary; no finding supplied
    `the Secretary finds that the requirements of participating States will exceed the appropriation`

-- src:2710 | In any fiscal year, the Secretary shall limit the value of those allotments issued to an amount not in excess of the appropriation for such fiscal year. Notwithstanding any other provision of this chapter, if in any fiscal year the Secretary finds that the requirements of participating States will exceed the appropriation, the Secretary shall direct State agencies to reduce the value of such allotments to be issued to households certified as eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program to the extent necessary to comply with the provisions of this subsection.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2027(b) (src:2710-2710)
GIVEN `the requirements of participating States for the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the appropriation for the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2027(b) the reduction in the value of the allotments to the extent necessary to comply with the subsection` MEANS
    -- reading: "to the extent necessary to comply with the provisions of this subsection" is the excess of the requirements over the appropriation, since the subsection's limit is the appropriation
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if ... the requirements of participating States will exceed the appropriation"; with no excess the text requires no reduction
    IF `the requirements of participating States for the fiscal year` GREATER THAN `the appropriation for the fiscal year`
        THEN JUST (`the requirements of participating States for the fiscal year` MINUS `the appropriation for the fiscal year`)
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2712 | In prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced under subsection (b) of this section, the Secretary shall ensure that such reductions reflect, to the maximum extent practicable, the ratio of household income, determined under sections 2014(d) and 2014(e) of this title, to the income standards of eligibility, for households of equal size, determined under section 2014(c) of this title. The Secretary may, in prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced, establish (1) special provisions applicable to persons sixty years of age or over and persons who are physically or mentally handicapped or otherwise disabled, and (2) minimum allotments after any reductions are otherwise determined under this section.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2027(c) (src:2712-2712)
GIVEN `the Secretary is prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2027(c) the Secretary is required to ensure that the reductions reflect the ratio of household income to the income standards of eligibility` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to the maximum extent practicable"; and only "In prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced under subsection (b)"
    IF `the Secretary is prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced under subsection (b)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2712 | In prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced under subsection (b) of this section, the Secretary shall ensure that such reductions reflect, to the maximum extent practicable, the ratio of household income, determined under sections 2014(d) and 2014(e) of this title, to the income standards of eligibility, for households of equal size, determined under section 2014(c) of this title. The Secretary may, in prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced, establish (1) special provisions applicable to persons sixty years of age or over and persons who are physically or mentally handicapped or otherwise disabled, and (2) minimum allotments after any reductions are otherwise determined under this section.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2027(c) (src:2712-2712)
GIVEN `s 2014(d) and (e) the household income, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `s 2014(c) the income standard of eligibility for households of equal size, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2027(c) the ratio of household income to the income standard of eligibility` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "the ratio of household income, determined under sections 2014(d) and 2014(e) of this title, to the income standards of eligibility, for households of equal size, determined under section 2014(c)"; a standard of nothing or less has no ratio
    IF `s 2014(c) the income standard of eligibility for households of equal size, in dollars` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN JUST (`s 2014(d) and (e) the household income, in dollars` DIVIDED BY `s 2014(c) the income standard of eligibility for households of equal size, in dollars`)
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2712 | In prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced under subsection (b) of this section, the Secretary shall ensure that such reductions reflect, to the maximum extent practicable, the ratio of household income, determined under sections 2014(d) and 2014(e) of this title, to the income standards of eligibility, for households of equal size, determined under section 2014(c) of this title. The Secretary may, in prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced, establish (1) special provisions applicable to persons sixty years of age or over and persons who are physically or mentally handicapped or otherwise disabled, and (2) minimum allotments after any reductions are otherwise determined under this section.
@ref 7 U.S.C. 2027(c) (src:2712-2712)
GIVEN person IS AN Individual
      `the person is physically or mentally handicapped or otherwise disabled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2027(c)(1) the Secretary may establish special provisions applicable to the person in prescribing the manner of reducing allotments` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "persons sixty years of age or over and persons who are physically or mentally handicapped or otherwise disabled"; the text does not speak of other persons
    IF person's `age in years` AT LEAST 60 OR `the person is physically or mentally handicapped or otherwise disabled` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2712 | In prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced under subsection (b) of this section, the Secretary shall ensure that such reductions reflect, to the maximum extent practicable, the ratio of household income, determined under sections 2014(d) and 2014(e) of this title, to the income standards of eligibility, for households of equal size, determined under section 2014(c) of this title. The Secretary may, in prescribing the manner in which allotments will be reduced, establish (1) special provisions applicable to persons sixty years of age or over and persons who are physically or mentally handicapped or otherwise disabled, and (2) minimum allotments after any reductions are otherwise determined under this section.
